---
/**
 * /changelog
 *
 * THREE THINGS CORRECTED IN THE PORT, all small and all measurable.
 *
 * 1. `<time>` HAD NO `datetime`. The legacy elements carry the ISO string as a
 *    text node only, so the date is not machine-readable. The one thing a
 *    <time> element exists to provide. Now emitted properly, and the visible
 *    text is formatted for a human while the attribute stays ISO.
 *
 * 2. THE HERO ADVERTISED CONTENT THE PAGE DOES NOT HAVE. Its eyebrow read
 *    "Changelog · System Status · UK Built"; there is no system status anywhere
 *    on the page. Removed rather than left as a promise the page breaks
 *    immediately. Anything that changes what a reader is told is de-claiming
 *    here, never adding.
 *
 * 3. A FALSE AFFORDANCE. "Explore the CrowAgent roadmap →" was styled as a link
 *    and was a plain <span>. Arrow, link colouring, no href. It is a real link
 *    now, to the destination it always implied.
 *
 * A third changelog entry exists on the legacy page only as an HTML comment
 * recording its removal (2026-07-28). Deliberately not ported.
 *
 * THE FEED IS STALE, and that is a content problem I cannot fix from here: the
 * newest entry is 2026-05-05 while the site shipped a homepage rebuild on
 * 2026-08-01 and removed five tools on 2026-07-28. A changelog three months
 * behind, under a standfirst reading "Every shipped change, in one feed",
 * undercuts its own claim. Logged as OA-14. Writing release notes is the
 * owner's call, not mine.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/layout/Section.astro';
import Button from '../components/ui/Button.astro';
import { breadcrumbs } from '../lib/schema';

const title = 'Changelog | CrowAgent';
const description = 'Public release notes for CrowMark. Every shipped change, in one feed.';

const schema = [
  breadcrumbs([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Changelog', path: '/changelog/' },
  ]),
];

interface Entry {
  /** ISO. Drives both the datetime attribute and the displayed date. */
  date: string;
  tag: string;
  heading: string;
  items: string[];
}

const ENTRIES: Entry[] = [
  {
    date: '2026-09-03',
    tag: 'CrowMark for Buyers',
    heading: 'Managing the contract after award, and PPN 026 by default',
    items: [
      'Supplier relationship management. A supplier profile now carries the commitments made in the winning bid, alongside scorecards, periodic review sessions and a risk radar, so what was promised at tender stays visible for the life of the contract.',
      'Concerns and corrective actions, each raised against the commitment it came from rather than kept in a separate log.',
      "A benefit and value realisation tracker, so the savings a contract was justified on are recorded against that contract instead of in somebody's spreadsheet.",
      'A due diligence workspace, a relationship feedback view for buyer teams, and procurement stages on every contract.',
      'You choose the social value model when you set up a contract. PPN 026 is now the default on new work, and PPN 002 stays selectable until 31 December 2026 for procurements already running under it, marked as retiring so nobody picks it by accident. The Cabinet Office has not yet published the PPN 026 sub criteria, which are expected in autumn 2026, so CrowMark does not score against them and will not pretend to.',
      'Sign in, sign up, password reset and multi-factor pages rebuilt to the approved design.',
      'Sessions now expire, with a seven day time box and a 24 hour inactivity limit on every account.',
    ],
  },
  {
    date: '2026-08-24',
    tag: 'CrowMark for Suppliers',
    heading: 'Review gates, version history and a briefing for the tender pack',
    items: [
      'Configurable review gates, with bid or no bid as gate zero, so a decision not to bid is recorded in the same place as a decision to go ahead.',
      'Answer history, diff and restore in the editor, plus track changes on the writing surface.',
      'A tender briefing that reads the pack, so a long invitation to tender can be understood before anybody starts writing.',
      'Pre-tender visibility: prior information notices, and framework or dynamic purchasing system expiry dates.',
      'Published award notices now feed the opportunity view, so past awards sit beside the tenders you are looking at.',
      'Buyer authored measure frameworks, a social value proxy calculator, and local indicators drawn from published sources.',
      'Salesforce and HubSpot inbound sync, and a read and write MCP server for teams who want CrowMark inside their own tooling.',
      'Document generation across eight surfaces, including the ISO 27001 pack rendered to branded Word documents.',
    ],
  },
  {
    date: '2026-07-26',
    tag: 'CrowMark for Suppliers',
    heading: 'Release 2.6: whole tender packs in, one editor, six stages',
    items: [
      'Upload the whole tender pack. ZIP archives are expanded into their child documents, and PowerPoint, Excel and CSV files are read as structured content rather than flattened to text.',
      'Email intake, so a tender pack can be forwarded straight into CrowMark.',
      'A six stage bid lifecycle replaced the old wizard, with tender first entry and a single answer editor in place of the two that came before it.',
      'The bid or no bid decision and the criteria behind it are persisted rather than lost once the bid starts.',
      'CPV codes on opportunities, and bill of quantities spreadsheets read row by row rather than sheet by sheet.',
      'Biometric sign in. Windows Hello and Touch ID can stand in for a typed authentication code, and one passkey covers both the app and the portal. Credentials are listed and revoked in settings.',
      'CrowAgent Core was retired and the portfolio repositioned around CrowMark.',
    ],
  },
  {
    date: '2026-05-05',
    tag: 'Marketing surface',
    heading: 'MP1: Marketing surface expansion',
    items: [
      'New /tools hub aggregating six free tools. All six have since been withdrawn: five in July 2026, and the social value calculator on 4 August 2026. The hub now carries the tender compliance matrix.',
      'New SEO landing page for the social value calculator, withdrawn 4 August 2026 and redirected to the PPN 026 glossary entry.',
      'New long-form methodology pages for each free tool, citing source regulation and edge cases.',
      'Top nav and footer extended with Free Tools surface.',
    ],
  },
  {
    date: '2026-04-26',
    tag: 'Infrastructure',
    heading: 'Cloudflare Pages migration complete',
    items: [
      'crowagent.ai now serves from Cloudflare Pages (project crowagent-website).',
      'Eliminated cross-repo deployment risk. Improved edge performance for UK users.',
    ],
  },
];

/* Sorted here rather than trusted to authoring order, so a new entry added in
   the wrong place cannot silently break reverse-chronology. */
const sorted = [...ENTRIES].sort((a, b) => b.date.localeCompare(a.date));

const fmt = (iso: string) =>
  new Date(iso).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });

const latest = sorted[0];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/changelog" schema={schema}>
  <Section
    as="h1"
    eyebrow="Changelog · UK built"
    title="What we shipped, and when."
    standfirst="Public release notes for CrowMark. Every shipped change, in one feed."
    id="changelog-hero"
  >
    {/* Derived from the entries, so it cannot disagree with the top of the list
        the way a hand-written "Latest:" line eventually would. */}
    <p class="meta latest">
      Latest: <strong>{latest.heading.split(':')[0]}, <time datetime={latest.date}>{fmt(latest.date)}</time></strong>
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Release notes" id="changelog-entries">
    <ol class="feed">
      {
        sorted.map((e) => (
          <li class="feed__item">
            <div class="feed__meta">
              <time class="meta feed__date" datetime={e.date}>
                {fmt(e.date)}
              </time>
              <span class="chip feed__tag">{e.tag}</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="feed__h">{e.heading}</h3>
              <ul class="feed__list">
                {e.items.map((i) => (
                  <li>{i}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </Section>

  <Section
    title="Ready to see what's next for CrowMark?"
    standfirst="The roadmap sets out what is being built, what is being researched, and what will not be built at all."
    id="changelog-cta"
  >
    <div class="btn-row">
      <Button href="/roadmap/">View roadmap</Button>
      <Button href="/pricing/" variant="secondary">Pricing</Button>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* CENTRED UNDER A CENTRED HEAD. Owner report, 2026-08-02: "central alignment
     is missing" on this page. Section centres the head block; the latest line,
     the feed track and the CTA row all sat left, so the page read as two
     layouts stacked. Alignment only, and the feed's own two-column grid keeps
     its internal left alignment because a date and a bullet list are not
     things to centre. */
  .latest {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--c-text-muted);
  }

  /* Weight is the shared `.meta` recipe; only the colour is local. */
  .latest strong { color: var(--c-ambient-start); }


  /* A narrower centred track rather than the full measure. At 1160px the
     220px meta column left a wide empty gutter beside every short entry, which
     is what made the feed read as detached from the heading above it. */
  .feed {
    list-style: none;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure-mid);
  }

  .feed__item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 220px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0 clamp(20px, 3vw, 44px);
    padding: var(--stack-2) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--c-border);
  }

  .feed__meta { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; align-items: flex-start; }

  .feed__date {
    color: var(--c-text-muted);
  }

  .feed__tag {
    color: var(--c-ambient-start);
  }

  .feed__h {
    margin: 0 0 var(--stack-1);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--t-h4);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--c-text);
  }

  .feed__list {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    list-style: disc;
  }

  .feed__list li {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--t-body);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--c-text-sub);
  }

  .feed__list li + li { margin-top: 6px; }
  .feed__list li::marker { color: var(--c-text-muted); }

  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    .feed__item { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 10px; }
    .feed__meta { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; gap: 12px; }
  }
</style>
